# Purity

`src/core` has **no DOM, no I/O, no Capacitor, no `Date`, no `Math.random`,
no `console`.** It imports only `src/core`.

Everything the engine needs arrives in the `GameState` it was handed, or in
the bundle bound to it. Nothing is read from the world at play time.

The lint enforces the mechanical half — `Math.random`, `new Date`, `Date.now`,
`process`, `console`, `document`, `window` and `localStorage` are restricted
syntax inside `src/core`. The lint is a floor, not the rule.

> "load" means validate, not read from disk. A `src/core` function takes the
> already-parsed value; the caller does the reading.
